  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2002-p16.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let the common value be \\(k.\\) Then \\(a=k-1,\\) \\(b=k-2,\\) \\(c=k-3,\\) \\(d=k-4,\\) so \\(a+b+c+d=4k-10.\\)\n\nSince \\(a+b+c+d+5=k,\\) we get \\(4k-10+5=k,\\) so \\(3k=5\\) and \\(k=\\dfrac{5}{3}.\\) Then \\(a+b+c+d=k-5\\) \\(=\\dfrac{5}{3}-5=-\\dfrac{10}{3}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Set every expression equal to a single value \\(k\\)",
        "Write \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) \\(c,\\) \\(d\\) in terms of \\(k\\) and add them"
      ],
